I made a very simple modification like this to my local copy of Nethack 
once.  I made it so that instead of the chance of leaving a bonesfile 
you would ALWAYS leave a bonesfile upon death (well, for eligible levels 
anyway), and in addition, loading a bonesfile didn't delete it.  The 
only modification I didn't make was always loading a bonesfile if it 
exists, but that wouldn't be too hard either.  You're looking at maybe 
editing 20 lines of code total.  Not too hard at all.

It was kind of an interesting experience, seeing the bonesfiles 
gradually accumulating in my directory and then starting to hit the same 
ones in successive games.


